# install/tool-versions.env — SINGLE SOURCE for the pinned OUT-OF-BAND tools.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Ubuntu 24.04 froze in April 2024, so a large slice of the shell stack is not in apt
# at all — or is there at a version Core cannot use. bootstrap.sh installs those from
# upstream. The naive way to do that is `curl … | sh`: unpinned, unverified, executed
# as the invoking user. That is not a supply chain, it is the absence of one. Core
# solved the same problem for its CI toolchain in core/scripts/tool-versions.env; this
# is that discipline applied to bootstrap.
#
# This repo leans on this file harder than any other in the fleet — that is the direct
# consequence of targeting an LTS rather than a rolling release, not a design choice.
#
# HOW IT IS USED
#   bootstrap.sh's `verified_install` / `verified_tree_install` read the *_VERSION and
#   *_SHA256 below, download the exact release ASSET (not the vendor's install script),
#   sha256sum -c it, and only then unpack. A pin that is missing, malformed, or
#   mismatched FAILS that tool's install and says so in the closing report — it never
#   silently falls through to an unverified path.
#
# SCOPE — Linux x86_64 (amd64) only, the same scope Core's pin file declares.
#   These hashes are per-architecture. On any other arch bootstrap.sh skips the
#   verified path and says so; install those tools by hand.
#
# BUMPING
#   Edit the *_VERSION here, then run `scripts/update-tool-checksums.sh` to refresh the
#   matching *_SHA256, and review the diff. A version bump without a checksum refresh is
#   an incomplete change: the download will fail closed.
#
# NOT LISTED HERE, ON PURPOSE
#   glow / gum        — Charm's signed apt repo (rotating signing key beats a hash we
#                       hand-maintain, and it is distro-agnostic where a PPA is not).
#   op (1Password)    — 1Password's signed apt repo, same reasoning.
#   yq / doggo / sesh — `go install` against the module proxy, which verifies against
#                       the checksum database.
#   yazi / viddy / ast-grep — NOT INSTALLED on this repo. They are cargo-only, and
#                       noble's rustc is 1.75 — too old to build them. All three are
#                       HAVE_*-guarded in Core, so the shell degrades cleanly without
#                       them. `mise use -g rust` then `cargo install --locked <tool>`
#                       if you want them on a particular box.
#
# Plain KEY=VALUE, no spaces around `=`, no `v` prefix — so this both `source`s in bash
# and is greppable by a single sed. Same format contract as Core's file.
# ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── the two that are NOT optional ─────────────────────────────────────────────

# neovim — noble ships 0.9.5. core/nvim pins nvim-treesitter to its `main` branch, which
# hard-requires 0.12 (see core/nvim/lua/gerrrt/config/providers.lua). Three minors short,
# and noble-backports has nothing. Installed as a TREE (bin/ + lib/ + share/nvim/runtime),
# not a lone binary — copying just bin/nvim yields an nvim with no runtime.
# Deliberately the tarball, not the AppImage: Ubuntu 24.04 sets
# kernel.apparmor_restrict_unprivileged_userns=1, which blocks the unprivileged user
# namespace an AppImage needs to FUSE-mount itself.
NVIM_VERSION=0.12.4
NVIM_SHA256=012bf3fcac5ade43914df3f174668bf64d05e049a4f032a388c027b1ebd78628

# tree-sitter CLI — nvim-treesitter needs >= 0.26.1 (core/PORTING-MATRIX.md footnote 5).
# noble has 0.20.8, trixie 0.22.6 — no Debian/Ubuntu suite short of sid clears the floor,
# so this one stays out-of-band for the foreseeable future. Ships as a plain .gz of the
# bare executable, NOT a tarball.
TREESITTER_VERSION=0.26.12
TREESITTER_SHA256=d00ac0daefc4bf8c4b57842a5c0509927232faad1d83157b64fbad4e2e8d9a8b

# ── absent from noble entirely ────────────────────────────────────────────────

# starship — the prompt. Kali takes the distro build; noble has no package at all.
STARSHIP_VERSION=1.26.0
STARSHIP_SHA256=321f0dd7af8340a5f2e6a8fec6538a04f617486f9ec70d878f91c09cd8deef22

# lazygit — Core ships `alias lg='lazygit'` and a `prefix + g` tmux popup
# unconditionally, so without this both are dead on this box.
# NB the asset says `linux` lowercase; the git tag has a `v`, the filename does not.
LAZYGIT_VERSION=0.64.1
LAZYGIT_SHA256=f8ea237c41f194cd799b48505518bfdaae4edf5a2ad6bd3d898e939785ee4532

# atuin — shell history. Its own installer hardcodes ~/.atuin/bin, appends an
# `atuin init` line to ~/.zshrc that fights Core's 00-tools.zsh, and prompts on a
# tty for history import. Installing the release binary avoids all three.
ATUIN_VERSION=18.19.0
ATUIN_SHA256=4d7559ada42407ee8ddc62349acf134dd297568d032c45a746a7aef8a6860648

# mise — runtime/tool version manager. Core's 00-tools.zsh activates it.
MISE_VERSION=2026.8.6
MISE_SHA256=cfe49784ec9683b38510846958cfecd9b59da84d4e8a38d18ffda19dc2941ead

# uv — Astral's Python package/project manager.
UV_VERSION=0.12.5
UV_SHA256=68a509da24b06b4223a1c0175fb5eb5bc79342b76cbeff0cfe51ac3f5b17b6b2

# ty — Astral's type checker. Installed via `uv tool install` when uv is present
# (uv verifies its own downloads); this pin is the no-uv fallback path.
TY_VERSION=0.0.72
TY_SHA256=11087394fa6aeac8d449bce42a30eb03fd76dd9ad8f38e69dd8004785d3f98b0

# dust — `du` replacement. The apt package elsewhere is `du-dust` (binary `dust`);
# installed from upstream the binary is plainly `dust`, so Core's du-dust→dust name
# resolution is a no-op on this box. That is expected, not drift.
DUST_VERSION=1.2.4
DUST_SHA256=707cfdbfb9d2dc536f8c3853815bbe98a01012f2772463835edae06816551160

# xh — HTTPie-style HTTP client. The musl asset is upstream's portable build.
XH_VERSION=0.26.2
XH_SHA256=8c53b6a23435754f9e2ea8ab8c0d0296a1921404b88132cf9b364ff6e8c22a6e

# procs — modern `ps`. Ships a .zip, not a tarball, and the zipped file does not carry
# the exec bit; verified_install handles both.
PROCS_VERSION=0.14.12
PROCS_SHA256=81964faf9d5cd0e9f399d5d0954fb6fe4d4d9f7d3cbec4507633df5a45b11713

# difftastic — structural git diff; the binary is `difft`, not `difftastic`. Opt-in
# (Core gates it on HAVE_DIFFT), so a skip here is harmless.
# NB this project's tags carry NO `v` prefix.
DIFFT_VERSION=0.70.0
DIFFT_SHA256=2997d2bbe620534edbd79b0049f00ce84eef3fedb15c7822456d58e38d8b05c9

# git-delta — Core's git pager, invoked as `delta`. In apt on noble and trixie as
# `git-delta`, but ABSENT from kali-rolling (proven by the kali packages lane), so it is
# `# skip:kali` in the manifest and arrives here instead. verified_install is
# `command -v delta`-guarded, so this fetch no-ops on the two distros where apt already
# supplied it and only fires on Kali. NB this project's tags carry NO `v` prefix.
DELTA_VERSION=0.18.2
DELTA_SHA256=99607c43238e11a77fe90a914d8c2d64961aff84b60b8186c1b5691b39955b0f

# hexyl — hex viewer; the stack's only binary-inspection verb. Same story as delta:
# in apt on noble and trixie, absent from kali-rolling. Core gates it on HAVE_HEXYL, so
# a skip is harmless, but an operator box is exactly where you want it. Tags DO carry a
# `v` prefix here, and the version appears in the asset name with it.
HEXYL_VERSION=0.17.0
HEXYL_SHA256=71b7463b8716225b4248525066e24b1874e954e87f397096f53e8804e3360189

# carapace — completions. Version only, no hash: it arrives as a .deb and apt verifies
# it on install. Deliberately NOT go-installed — `go install` cannot work for any
# version of it (replace directives in go.mod plus uncommitted generated sources).
CARAPACE_VERSION=1.7.3
